{%- comment -%}
  A section eyebrow — the small label that sits above a heading.

  Renders nothing when the eyebrow only repeats the heading it labels. The v4
  copy pass gave several sections a heading identical to the eyebrow already in
  place ("How they work" over "How they work"), which reads as a mistake rather
  than a label. Guarding here rather than blanking the settings means a
  generator re-run, a theme-editor save, or the next copy pass cannot bring the
  duplicate back.

  The comparison ignores case and a trailing full stop, because the headings
  take one and eyebrows never do.

  Accepts:
  - eyebrow: {String} The label. Required — nothing renders without it.
  - heading: {String} The heading it sits above. Optional.
  - class:   {String} Extra classes for the element. Optional.

  Usage:
  {% render 'hs-eyebrow', eyebrow: section.settings.eyebrow, heading: section.settings.heading %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign eyebrow_key = eyebrow | strip | downcase | strip_html | replace: '’', "'"
  assign heading_key = heading | strip | downcase | strip_html | replace: '’', "'"
  if heading_key ends_with '.'
    assign heading_key = heading_key | remove_last: '.'
  endif
-%}
{%- if eyebrow != blank and eyebrow_key != heading_key -%}
  <p class="hs-eyebrow{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
{%- endif -%}
